{"duration_api_ms":4813,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"36bb3fef-4fd1-4a69-81ab-a38668323027","total_cost_usd":0.0006459,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":695,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":740,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":381},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":695,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":740,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":695,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":695},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1239,"outputTokens":766,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":695,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0006459,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":381,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":695,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**No.** Historical share volume shows how much has traded, not how much a new order can trade without moving the price. For ETFs, liquidity also depends on the underlying basket.\n\n**Creation/redemption:** Authorized participants (APs) exchange baskets of underlying securities for creation units (typically 25,000 to 100,000 shares) and back again. This arbitrage links secondary-market prices to NAV, so the ETF's liquidity can draw on the underlying market, not just its own trading.\n\n**Additional indicators to examine:**\n- **Quoted spread and displayed depth** at the NBBO, plus realized effective spreads\n- **Premium/discount to iNAV**, which signals stress or dislocation\n- **Underlying liquidity:** bid-ask spreads and trading volume of holdings, especially for bonds or small caps\n- **Number of market makers and APs**\n- **Creation/redemption activity** and shares outstanding\n- **Closing auction and intraday volume patterns**\n\nThese are observable conditions, not guarantees. Actual fill quality for your order depends on market conditions at execution.","ttft_ms":2548,"type":"result","duration_ms":4241,"uuid":"11072e51-73c3-40d4-8afd-83b6ea71d34d","ttft_stream_ms":485,"time_to_request_ms":87,"first_content_frame_ms":485,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
